    LLM: 'Game: German Solo. Use 32-card deck, run contract bidding, apply fixed matador trump hierarchy, follow suit in 8 tricks, and settle bid outcomes.',
    Player: 'German Solo: bid a realistic contract, remember fixed matadors, and play tricks to contract target.',
    objective: 'As bidder or bidder side, complete contract trick target; as defenders, set the contract.',
    gameplay: 'Players bid once in turn with higher contracts over lower. Some contracts create a temporary partner via called ace or king; others are solo contracts. Winning bid determines trump suit and contract objective. Play 8 tricks with follow-suit required. If void in led suit, player may trump or discard. Highest trump wins trick; otherwise highest of led suit. Trick winner leads next.',
    keyRules: [
      'Matador order is fixed: club queen highest, then seven of trump, then spade queen, followed by remaining trump hierarchy.',
      'Contracts form a ladder and determine target tricks, trump regime, and whether bidder plays alone or with called partner.',
      'Each player bids at most once per hand in the common four-player form.',
      'Settlement is by bid value transfer with optional table bonuses such as mackers and first-and-last.',
